  <!-- ===== TODO 5: Image best practices checklist ===== -->
  <!-- Task: Read through these practices and think about why each matters:
       1. ALWAYS include descriptive alt text (helps screen readers and SEO)
       2. Choose the right file format (JPG for photos, PNG for graphics)
       3. Optimize file size (compress images to load faster)
       4. Use width/height attributes (reserves space, prevents layout shift)
       5. Make images scale to the screen (the style attribute from TODO 3)
  -->
  <section id="practices">
    <h2>Image Best Practices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Alt text:</strong> Describe the image for screen readers and accessibility</li>
      <li><strong>File format:</strong> Use JPG for photos, PNG for graphics with transparency, SVG for icons</li>
      <li><strong>File size:</strong> Compress images to improve page loading speed</li>
      <li><strong>Width/Height:</strong> Define dimensions to prevent layout shift when image loads</li>
      <li><strong>Scaling:</strong> The style attribute can make images shrink to fit small screens (CSS, coming in Lesson 05)</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

